# v1465 — per-install identity: unique per PC, must NEVER travel between machines
# v2119 — AND THE ROOT COPIES. These two patterns name `tv/` only, so `git check-ignore` was
# silent on `/.tvd_identity.json` and `git add -A` staged it into a PUBLIC repo, carrying this
# machine's install id, its hostname and its username. Anyone cloning inherited konyo-3.local's
# identity as their own. [[the-unjoined-end]]
/.tvd_identity.json
/.tvd_beacon.json
tv/.tvd_identity.json

# v2146 — WHICH WORLD THE BOARD CAME BACK AS. Same class as .tvd_identity.json directly above, and
# nearly the same near-miss: v2145 added this file and did NOT ignore it, so the first time the
# console wrote it a `git add -A` would have staged a per-install identity into a PUBLIC repo — the
# exact thing the note above records happening once already. Caught by a cross-family review before
# the file was ever written. The .tmp is the atomic-write partner and must go too.
tv/.board_identity.json
tv/.board_identity.json.tmp
# v1597 — the beacon's own last-result record. Per-install and machine-specific (attempts,
# failures, the IP-dependent verdict), exactly like .tvd_identity.json beside it. Committing
# it would push one machine's beacon history onto every other machine that pulls.
tv/.tvd_beacon.json

# scratch probes used while debugging — never ship
_forgecheck.html
_measure.html
_probe.html
_seed*.html
_ls*.html
_lsfork_probe.html

# v1481 — runtime state the launcher writes, not source. start_tvd_win.ps1 caches the
# "webview imports cleanly" probe result here so every launch does not re-pay it; the value is
# true for THIS machine's python only, so committing it would hand another machine a stale answer
# about an interpreter it does not have.
tv/.webview_ok
_freshpc_probe.html
_sigil_probe.html
_worlds_probe.html
# v1524 — per-machine sweep memory: which sealed reels the Chronicle sweep has already read.
# Machine-local by nature (his Mac and the Windows cousin have different footage) and worthless
# to anyone else, so it never travels.
tv/chronicle_swept.json
# v2184 — the hunt's memory of which PAID hunts came back empty. Same reason as the line above:
# it is live state, it names items off his own reels, and this repo is PUBLIC. I created it in
# v2174 and did not add it here, so `git add -A` swept the running console's copy into a public
# commit within hours. Every path in run_gates._LIVE_STATE is now required to be ignored, by a
# test, because remembering is not a mechanism.
tv/chron_hunt_memory.json
tv/auto_relaunch.json
# v2189 — the board's own tally, handed over by bible.html so the fleet numbers work on Windows
# too. Live state, and it names his progress: never committed to a PUBLIC repo.
tv/board_tally.json
tv/shadow_ledger.json
tv/.render_shots/

# v1711 — the G5 stats ledger is per-machine runtime counters, like the budget file
tv/g5_stats.json

# v1777 — the accumulated sighting ledger is LIVE MACHINE STATE, not source. It is rewritten
# every ten pages during a sweep; tracking it would make every run a noisy diff and would put one
# machine.s reading history into a public repo.
tv/chron_evidence.json
tv/chron_evidence.json.tmp
# 2026-08-20 — the console's LAST SWEEP RESULT is live state, not source. It was tracked
# from v1763 and rode along in 22 commits, churning 610KB of his grail into a PUBLIC repo
# on every sweep, while its two siblings above were ignored from the start. run_gates
# already lists it in _LIVE_STATE — the fingerprint that catches a TEST writing his console
# — so the tree already treats it as live state; only git had not been told.
tv/chron_last_result.json
tv/chron_last_result.json.tmp
tv/chron_autoread.json
tv/chron_autoread.json.tmp
tv/chron_reads.json
tv/vault_last_result.json
tv/chron_reads.json
tv/vault_last_result.json.tmp

# v1780 — a running sweep declares itself here; machine state, never source
tv/.sweep.lock

# v1941 — derived gate verdicts for sealed frames; machine state, never source
tv/stash_gate_cache.json
tv/stash_gate_cache.json.tmp

# v2047 — MACHINE STATE THAT HOLDS HIS DATA. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC AND A PUSH PUBLISHES.
# vault_accum.json was committed EMPTY as scaffolding at v1884 and has been tracked ever since.
# After a real sweep it holds item NAMES, frame ids, session ids and witness counts — his vault.
# It survived tonight only because every `git add` named explicit paths; one `git add -A` would
# have published it. Machine state is not source. [[feedback-fixtures-never-touch-live-data]]
tv/vault_accum.json
tv/vault_seen.json
tv/vault_swept.json
